/public/storage
# Nothing from storage/ ships in the repository. The subdirectories carry their
# own ignore files, but storage/ itself did not, which is how an
# installed.lock - the "this system is already set up" marker - was committed
# and then cloned into every new deployment, closing the install wizard on
# machines nobody had installed. Tracked files stay tracked; this stops new
# runtime artefacts from being added by accident.
/storage/*
!/storage/app/
!/storage/debugbar/
!/storage/framework/
!/storage/logs/
# Where tools/release/build-package.sh writes a release package by default.
# These are build output - a 30 MB tarball per release - and two of them were
# committed by accident on 2026-11-08, taking the repository's tracked content
# from 28 MB to 88 MB and ending up inside the next release package, which has
# no business carrying the previous ones. They are published as GitHub release
# assets, never tracked here.
/dist
/vendor
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
.env.testing
AGENTS.md

# merge leftovers (git mergetool, patch)
*.orig
*.rej
*.revbak
